{
  "name": "CS452-LAB2",
  "description": "An OpenGL 3.3 core profile implementation focusing on hardware-accelerated rendering through Vertex Array Objects (VAOs) and Vertex Buffer Objects (VBOs) in legacy Rust. The project implements a programmable graphics pipeline utilizing GLSL shaders to render complex primitives, including a Sierpinski gasket point cloud and stochastic line distributions. It demonstrates foundational graphics programming techniques by abstracting shader compilation and buffer management while strictly avoiding deprecated immediate-mode APIs.",
